

JDK : Java Development Kit

JRE : Java Runtime Environment

JVM : Java Virtual Machine(Interpreter of Java)
	-Compiled Language(c,c++)
	-Interpreted Language(java,python)

API : Application Programing Interface(library)


JDK	: API + Compiler +JVM

JRE	: API + JVM




Data Types : 

1)Primitive
	-byte
	-short
	-int
	-long
	-char
	-float
	-double
	-boolean	
2)Non-Primitive
	-Array
	-Class
	-Interface
	
Primitive Data Types : 
1)Integer (123,-250)
	-byte
	-short
	-int
	-long
2)Floating Point(45.23,-567.23)
	-float
	-double

3)Character('a','A','@','4')
	-char
	
4)Boolean(true/false)
	-boolean
	


Integer : 
keyword		memory		range
-byte			1 byte			-128, 0, +127

-short			2 bytes			-32768, 0, +32767

-int				4 bytes			-/+ 10 digits 

-long  			8 bytes			-/+ 19 digits 


Character:
-char			2 bytes			0, 65535

Character Code : 
c/c++ : ASCII 1 byte
(American Standerd code for information interchanged)

Java : Uni Code 2 byte
0, 255 - English Characters

Floating Point:
-float			4 bytes			-/+ 10 digits

-double			8 bytes			-/+19 digits

Note : In java all floating point constants are double type by default.

c/c++ :

float f = 1.5; ok
		float

Java : 
float f = 1.5; error
		double
float f = 1.5f; ok
float f = (float)1.5; ok
doube f = 1.5; ok

Boolean : 
-boolean		1 byte			true/false

boolean b = true;







